  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Word stress",
     "texto": [
      "In many Norwegian words the stress falls on the first syllable, but loanwords can follow other patterns. The stressed syllable stands out from the unstressed ones.",
      "Norwegian has two lexical tones in many dialects. The exact form varies between regions and is not marked in writing; that is why it is learned by listening to specific words and speakers."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
